  "//deps": "Consumer runtime deps = the vendored library (file:) + EVERY runtime dependency the library imports. ALL library runtime deps are listed here because the deploy pipeline (C3 Studio, test dirs) runs `npm install` ONLY in ui/react/ — it never installs inside ui/agentix-chat-ui/, so that dir's node_modules is empty in the real environment and bare imports from the library source (clsx, class-variance-authority, radix-ui, tiptap extensions, marked, dompurify, etc.) would fail to resolve. Listing them all here makes a single `npm install` in ui/react/ self-sufficient. The singletons among them are additionally pinned in vite.config.mts so they resolve to a single physical copy. On a library upgrade, reconcile this dep list against the new library package.json at ui/agentix-chat-ui/package.json (union of its dependencies + peerDependencies + this file: dep — react/react-dom/react-router/i18next/react-i18next are peers the consumer supplies here, react-router as v7 on React 18 or v8 on React 19), not just the singleton list (see CLAUDE.md 'Upgrading the embedded chat library').",
